  "subject": "🎶 Axios Finish Line: Sonic seasoning",
  "date": "Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:29:25 -0400",
  "body_text": "96 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n 🦌 Plus: View at Hurricane Ridge | Tuesday, October 27, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n View in browser \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n Axios Finish Line \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n By Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei &middot; Oct 27, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n Welcome back! Smart Brevity™ count: 311 words … 1 min. Copy edited by Amy Stern. \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 1 big thing: Taste of music \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios\n\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n There's a secret ingredient that can make anything you cook taste better: your favorite song.\n\n Scientists have discovered that what we hear while we eat can change the way our brains experience flavor. Why it matters: Our brains don't experience sights, sounds and tastes in isolation. Instead, our senses are constantly working together to shape how we perceive the world.\n\n 🍽️ Zoom in: Researchers at the University of Copenhagen used brain scans to observe people tasting sweet and sour foods while listening to music.\n\n They found that listening while tasting activated certain parts of the brain more intensely than tasting alone. 💛 The intrigue: Researchers say the findings could have implications for people dealing with a range of health issues.\n\n Consider head and neck cancer patients who've lost some of their sense of taste, or people recovering from eating disorders who are working to rebuild their relationship with food. Music could potentially help make eating a more enjoyable experience for them. The bottom line: Janice Wang, a co-author of the study, said in a release , \"This tells us flavor is not simply a property of food. Flavor is an experience created by the brain.\"\n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\nA MESSAGE FROM AXIOS\r\n\n \r\n See what's next for media in 2027 \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n Media Trends Executive Annual members receive the 2026 Annual Report, our special media document featuring global forecasts, sector analysis and exclusive media data insights.\r\n\n\r\n \r\n🔒 Get the report by becoming a Media Trends Executive member.\r\n\n\r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 2. 🏕️ Parting shot! \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Photo: Bill Rapai This photo of mule deer at Hurricane Ridge in Olympic National Park in Washington was taken by reader Bill Rapai of Grosse Pointe, Mich., a couple weeks ago.\n\n He writes: \"That's the Olympic Mountain Range in the background. We had just completed hiking one trail when these guys showed up near the parking lot. I followed them for a while, keeping a respectful distance, to get an image where the background was not full of cars and asphalt. I got my chance when they headed up this incline and fell into single file — just for me!\" \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n 🏁 Please invite your friends to join Finish Line . \n\n \r\n 👆 Like this comms style and format? It's called Smart Brevity®. Bring it to your org — via hands-on training or internal comms software — to harness its power and impact. \r\n &nbsp; Axios thanks our partners for supporting our journalism.\n Advertise with us. \n\n Read more about Axios' mission , ethics and how we use AI in our journalism . You can reach the authors by replying to this email.\nSponsorship has no influence on editorial content.\n\n Thank you for signing up for this Axios newsletter. To stop receiving this newsletter, unsubscribe or manage your email preferences . If someone forwarded this to you, sign up now to get Axios in your inbox.\n\n Axios, PO Box 101060, Arlington VA 22201 &nbsp; Follow Axios across:\n\n &nbsp; &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;",
